# Navigation and messages

Both shells (`base_management.html`, `base_employee.html`) use htmx `hx-boost`: links and
forms swap `<body>` without a full reload. Toasts sit in the top corner (left in Arabic,
right in English). Most of this is automatic. `core/tests_ui_conventions.py` enforces the
rest, so run it after UI changes.

## Already automatic (no extra code needed)
- Links and forms on new pages are boosted.
- Download and export links (`download`, `.csv/.xlsx/.pdf/...`, `/export/`, `/media/`) do a real navigation.
- `onsubmit="return confirm(...)"` and `hx-confirm` open the in-app confirm dialog (`window.rdConfirm`), not the browser dialog. `onclick="return false"` still cancels.
- `alert(...)` shows an error toast.
- Unsaved-form prompts and server or network error toasts work.
- Plain `{{ form.non_field_errors }}` becomes a toast.
- `document`/`window`/`body` listeners and `setInterval` added by a page script are removed when you leave the page (`static/js/page-scope.js`).
- `htmx.onLoad` callbacks registered by page scripts are removed when you leave the page.
- Don't add "bind once" guards like `if (window.__x) return;`: they break re-binding.

## Rules
- Every page `{% extends %}` one of the two shells. Don't write a new `<body>`.
- User feedback goes through Django messages in the view (`messages.success/error`).
  Never loop over `messages` in a page, and never use `alert-success`/`alert-danger` boxes.
- Form-wide errors:
  `{% include "partials/form_errors_toast.html" with errors=form.non_field_errors %}`.
  Field errors stay under their fields.
- Persistent state notes may use `alert-warning` / `alert-info`. A danger box that is real
  page content (for example inside a modal) needs `data-rd-inline-alert`.
- JS feedback: `window.rdToast(message, "success" | "error")`.
  JS navigation: `window.rdNavigate(url)`. Not `location.href = ...`.
- Page scripts must initialise on every visit. Use `htmx.onLoad(fn)` for element setup
  (it also covers htmx partial swaps).
- htmx partial endpoints: messages added in the view arrive as toasts automatically
  (via an `HX-Trigger` header).

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
{% for message in messages %}<div class="alert alert-success">{{ message }}</div>{% endfor %}
<!-- ✅ nothing in the template; in the view: -->
<!-- messages.success(request, _("Saved.")) -->
```

Visual identity (tokens, badges, fonts, buttons): see `.cursor/rules/pearl-ui.mdc` and `DESIGN.md`.
